# msort: merge sort of 12 integers by recursion; cell 0 the board (show, merge, msort), cell 1 the run; a breakpoint at the last line of merge (line 41 of cell 0) stops at each of the 11 merges, the stops read from a model of the algorithm (mk_msort.py); i and j are read, k is not (a for loop leaves its variable undefined). THE LAW as in queens.steps: next steps over a call, out stops in the caller at the line after the call.
{"break": [0, 41]}
{"run": 0, "expect": {"stopped": false}}
{"run": 1, "expect": {"cell": 0, "line": 41, "frames": [["merge", 41], ["msort", 51], ["msort", 49], ["msort", 49], ["msort", 49], ["main", 13]], "vars": {"lo": "1", "mid": "1", "hi": "2", "i": "2", "j": "3"}, "output": "before:   7   1   8   2   9   3  10   4  11   5  12   6\n"}}
